WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.300
Anchors away and put on a happy face,

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:05.780
because we have episode 5
of "American Horror Story".

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:13.160
In this video, we'll be
breaking down the latest episode,

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:15.900
and you'll want to stick around
to the very end for my theory on

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:18.540
why some ghosts are
reborn at Camp Redwood,

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:20.740
and why there are some we never see.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.940
So heads up, because here we go.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:29.760
The episode begins in 1980, four years before
Brooke and the gang arrive at Camp Redwood.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:34.620
We are here with Nurse Rita, or as we've
come to learn in episode 3, Donna Chambers.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:37.840
And for the purposes of this video,
I'm just gonna keep calling her Rita.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.940
She's on a stakeout, trying to find out
where her father has been disappearing to,

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:44.620
after her mother told her
that he's been sneaking out.

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:49.820
And judging by the amount of cigarette butts outside
her car, Rita has been here for quite some time.

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:55.540
For those of you really paying attention, Rose Royce's "Love Don't Live Here Anymore" plays in the background,

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:00.440
which has such lines as "You abandoned me", foreshadowing the death of her father.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:05.720
And speaking of her father, we see him get
out with a woman who definitely isn't Rita's mom.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:12.160
Rita demands that her father open the door,
thinking that some hanky-panky is happening,

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.220
but something far worse is on the other side:

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:18.100
the mutilated body
of her father's victim.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:21.860
Now Rita has some balls, instead of
getting the hell out of there, she's like,

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.500
"Man, I gotta check this shit out."

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:27.600
On the wall are conveniently
Polaroids of all of her father's kills.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:31.220
Men, women, black, white, it doesn't matter to him.

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:35.280
And around the room, you may have
noticed that he keeps mementos of his kills,

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:39.120
like earrings, ties, belts, handkerchiefs, and sunglasses.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:43.840
When the mutilated woman so rudely
interrupts Rita, she tries to stop the bleeding.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:45.840
Um, Rita, her intestines are out.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:48.120
Before she's interrupted by dad.

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:50.960
And I love how this brand of
bleach is just called "Bleach".

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:55.400
We learn that David, Rita's father,
has spent his entire life as a killer.

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:58.960
And what he's about to say starts
Rita on her journey to prove that

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:02.700
serial killing is learned, not
something that you're born with.

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:16.380
Rita only knows the father who loved and
raised her as a child, not this evil psychopath.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:21.840
She doesn't want to believe someone she
loves so much can be capable of so much evil.

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:26.100
She does disclose to him that she's a psychologist,
so I think we can put to rest theories that

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:30.600
she was lying about being one when
she first went to meet Jingles in episode 3.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:33.160
She tells him he
has the ability to change.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:36.640
But before she can change his mind,
he stabs himself in the neck.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:41.680
This whole intro section gives us
valuable insight into Rita's motivations.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:46.220
She wants to prove to everyone that killers
can change, that they can be redeemed.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:51.400
It's the same speech she gave to Jingles in
episode 3, telling him it's not his fault.

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:56.820
Society, war, trauma, play crucial roles in
whether someone will be a killer or not.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:59.980
We also saw this echoed with
Richard Ramirez's backstory.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:06.160
He's constantly traumatized as a child, even
witnessing his cousin kill his wife right in front of him.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:11.840
If Rita can prove her theory right, she herself
gets her own redemption and peace of mind.

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:16.080
She so wants to believe some
external factor made her dad kill

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:21.400
that she's willing to release a serial killer
from jail just in order to prove her point.

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:24.180
It's really messed up and I'm here for it.

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:29.160
We're back where last episode left off with Rita
having seen Ricky resurrect from the dead.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:39.260
He tells her that he was raised by the Unholy One,
and that Satan showed him everything about her,

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:40.980
how she released Mr. Jingles,

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:46.100
which led to the deaths of several counselors,
pranksters, and even a porn producer.

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:49.420
He calls into question her
very reason for being here,

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:53.560
contradicting her theory by
saying that evil is born within you.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:55.540
The ghost of her father even says,

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:03.680
Meaning if he was evil, it would
pass on to her. She is his seed.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:08.420
He then asks her to follow in his footsteps,
so it'll be interesting to see if she does.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:12.260
It's also interesting to note
here that Ricky doesn't kill Rita,

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:16.020
which leaves me wondering
if this was at Satan's behest.

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:20.920
We've seen striking similarities between
Ricky and season eight's Michael Langdon,

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:24.540
but no hard connection
other than Satan between the two.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:29.420
Outside the burning wreckage of the porn
producer's car, Xavier goes full psycho,

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:33.880
telling everyone that they need to burn
everything as some sort of signal fire.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:38.220
And it's ironic he's obsessed with fire,
since he was put in an oven last episode.

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:40.980
He's knocked out by Margaret,
who says he could harm someone,

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:44.100
but knowing that Margaret
was the secret killer all this time,

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:48.200
she's likely making excuses to
get some more kills under her belt.

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:52.240
Back in the cabin, the others decide what
to do next, with Margaret taking control.

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:56.980
Notice how she still has the gun,
conveniently out of bullets, according to her.

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:00.380
And the deer antlers, which make her
look like some sort of horned demon.

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:04.640
Of course, they decide the stupidest
plan of action, which is to yet again split up,

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:06.580
and who do they make go with Margaret?

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:14.320
Yes, the guy who just a few hours ago was impaled
with a spike and had to be resuscitated with adrenaline.

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:19.240
So Chet and Margaret head off, leaving Brooke
and Montana alone with a passed out Xavier.

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:23.320
Montana grabs a hatchet and is
about to kill Brooke, but she chickens out.

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:25.660
Remember that Montana wants Brooke dead

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:29.260
because she believes her responsible
for the death of her brother Sam.

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:34.720
Brooke runs out after seeing Ray, who we
know was decapitated at the end of episode 3.

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:41.360
If you recall, Ray's last line at the end of the episode was, "Suck a nut Camp Redwood, see you in another life".

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:45.860
Well, another life sounds about right,
as Ray has mysteriously come back to life.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:51.180
And he shows the same symptom as the
hitchhiker from episode 1: a loss of memory.

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:55.880
Chet and Margaret row, row, row their boat,
and at least Margaret didn't make him row.

00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:59.760
Hey, on the bright side, Chet, you now
probably qualify for the Paralympics.

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:01.420
Margaret gets on the topic of death,

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:05.500
probably not the best thing to discuss
after multiple people have been murdered,

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:10.279
but she wants to know if Chet will repent
and ask for forgiveness before she kills him.

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:14.140
He doesn't, and then we get the most
brutal paddle scene since "Animal House".

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:16.360
"Thank you, sir, may I have another?"

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:19.740
She attaches an anchor to his legs
and makes sure to cut off his ear

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:23.380
to keep up the charade that it's
Jingles responsible for these deaths.

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:27.120
Ray and Brooke have headed to the
cafeteria in the hopes of evading Jingles,

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:28.480
who they've heard in the woods.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:32.300
Remember that Jingles mysteriously
vanished after Margaret shot him,

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:36.220
but with Ricky and Ray coming back
from the dead, who the hell knows now.

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:39.660
Now, this scene doesn't offer a lot in
the way of moving the plot forward,

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:43.060
but we do get a lot of character
development for Ray and Brooke,

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:46.460
even a little kiss between the two,
which I predicted in episode 1.

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:50.640
Brooke tells us that she always had
to fake who she was in order to fit in.

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:53.260
That's how she met
Joseph Cavanaugh, her fiancé.

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:55.960
Even telling Ray that
she never really loved him,

00:06:56.260 --> 00:07:02.080
which calls into question if she actually did sleep with Sam, Montana's brother, the night before the wedding.

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:03.240
I like to think she didn't.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:07.560
And the two do what any sane people
would do during a killer rampage: bang.

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:11.400
Rita arrives to the cabin after being
scared shitless by Richard Ramirez,

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:15.040
and lets it out of the bag that
she was the one to release Jingles.

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:18.060
Xavier is pissed because his career is ruined,

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:20.580
although there is still
that porno of his around.

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:26.320
Rita says that if they can get to her car stashed away
in the staff parking lot, they may be able to get away.

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:30.760
But Xavier attacks, jeopardizing a
career for him, even in radio.

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:33.160
We see Ray and Brooke post ghost sex.

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:38.000
Now is it just me or was Brooke not too
thrilled about her first sexual encounter?

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:40.420
You know what they say:
Once you go ghost ...

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:45.720
She goes to the fridge, still thirsty, only to
find Ray's decapitated head from episode 3.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:47.720
And after finding it, she tells Ray,

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:54.760
Now, this is important, because in traditional
slasher films, the virgin always survives.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:57.260
But we just found out
she lost her V-card.

00:07:57.560 --> 00:08:01.500
But is it really losing your
V-card if you have sex with a ghost?

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:03.660
So keep that in mind as we go along.

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:06.480
Brooke runs back to the cabin
and we stumble upon Montana,

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:09.900
who looks to be preparing a tent.
She's wanting to make her getaway.

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:13.220
Brooke tells Montana about Ray, but
before she can barely get a word out,

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:15.840
Montana smashes in
her face with a flashlight.

00:08:15.980 --> 00:08:19.260
It's 20 minutes till sunrise and
as predicted in my last video,

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:21.680
because this episode
is entitled "Red Dawn",

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:25.600
we'll likely be seeing the rise of a
bloody new day at Camp Redwood.

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:30.120
Montana beats the crap out of Brooke
and finally reveals her true intentions,

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:32.480
showing us how she saw
her at Perfect 10 Aerobics,

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:35.560
and that she was the one to
give Richard Ramirez his blade.

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:39.420
We also get another brief discussion
on whether Montana had it in her to kill,

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:44.500
which echoes the question this season is
posing on whether people are born with evil or not.

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:53.980
And Montana is introduced to one
of my favorite bands: Radiohead.

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:03.220
Rita runs into the nursing station to
escape Xavier, when she runs into Jingles.

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:08.180
He's not too happy he's been brought here, taking
out bullets from his last encounter with Margaret.

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:11.520
Rita reiterates the driving
force of all her decisions.

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:21.280
And this question is
answered with Jingles.

00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:23.880
He was never a killer,
outside the war, at least.

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:27.840
It was Margaret and the mental
institution that turned him into this monster.

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:31.980
Not wanting to live with the guilt of
what she's done, she asks him to kill her.

00:09:32.180 --> 00:09:35.160
But Jingles knows it'll
be worse for Rita if she's alive.

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:42.340
Montana has gone full psycho, seems to be a recurring theme this season, and battles it out with Brooke,

00:09:42.340 --> 00:09:45.720
when we stumble upon Margaret
and Jingles at the archery range.

00:09:45.820 --> 00:09:48.520
He's not too pleased that she's
been pinning all these murders on him,

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:50.820
and just when it seems
like he'll have his revenge,

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:53.640
Xavier shoots him with
a shitload of arrows.

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:03.240
When he goes over to check on
Margaret, he's brutally stabbed by her,

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:06.840
which makes me wonder: If he comes
back to life, will he still have those burns?

00:10:06.860 --> 00:10:09.840
And will he make a deal with
the devil to get his life back?

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.840
And that seems to be what's
happening with Ricky and Jingles here.

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:18.100
Ricky is offering him a deal:
accept Satan as his master to be reborn.

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:23.880
Hallelujah, it's finally morning at Camp Redwood,
after almost 4 episodes completely set at night.

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:25.720
The kids have arrived for camp and

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:28.500
holy crap, Montana and
Brooke are still fighting.

00:10:28.680 --> 00:10:31.320
Brooke ends up killing
Montana in front of the children,

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:33.760
and Margaret pins all
the murders on Brooke.

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:38.740
Now this is interesting, because she probably knows that Jingles has made some sort of deal with Ricky.

00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:45.120
She was there at the archery range and that pinning it all on him may not work anymore since well, he's not there.

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:47.320
Brooke is the next logical choice.

00:10:47.420 --> 00:10:50.300
As police and emergency
services arrive at Camp Redwood,

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:53.500
Brooke is taken away,
and Ray's blood pressure is taken.

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:55.700
But since he's dead, there's no reading.

00:10:55.760 --> 00:11:00.200
Forensics finds Ray's head in the fridge, and
when he's taken off Camp Redwood's property,

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:03.900
he's magically brought back,
unable to leave the grounds.

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:07.720
Now, whether or not his physical body
leaves the grounds we're not sure,

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:11.940
but it looks as though there's a distinction
between ghosts like Jonas Shevoore,

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:15.440
aka Jason Voorhees if you
rearrange the letters in his name,

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:17.340
and that of Ricky and Jingles.

00:11:17.620 --> 00:11:21.060
Why is it that Ricky and Jingles
get to leave but not the others?

00:11:21.260 --> 00:11:25.900
The clue lies in Ricky's earlier question
to Jingles: Would he accept Satan?

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:30.660
Perhaps in return for accepting Satan, you
are allowed to leave Camp Redwood reborn.

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:36.680
And if you don't or aren't even offered, you stay at
Camp Redwood in what Montana calls "purgatory".

00:11:36.680 --> 00:11:40.740
Also, bonus points if you caught the
Ghostbusters reference, a 1984 movie,

00:11:40.960 --> 00:11:44.460
when Montana says, "There 
is no Montana. Only Zuul."

00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:48.320
The episode also leaves us with
Ricky and Jingles off to Los Angeles.

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:52.180
Now, my best guess as to where
they're going is the satanic cult.

00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:58.700
In season 8, Michael stumbles across this cult in Los Angeles, so it seems like the logical place they would go.

00:11:58.940 --> 00:12:04.840
We also don't know where Rita went. Her work isn't done, and she's struggling with all the deaths she has caused.

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:08.980
Perhaps she will now seek her own
redemption and try to go after Jingles.

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:13.140
And this theme of redemption may
just be what it takes for our campers

00:12:13.180 --> 00:12:16.060
to release them from
this cycle of purgatory.

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:19.140
Every character who has
come back as a ghost so far

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:22.880
has some sort of traumatic past
they want to be redeemed from.

00:12:23.060 --> 00:12:26.540
This is why we see some people
return as ghosts and some not.

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:31.020
And I'm sure this isn't the last we'll see of Brooke,
who was seen being taken away by police.

00:12:31.320 --> 00:12:35.880
Episode 5 puts a whole new spin on the show
with characters branching out from Camp Redwood,

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:39.540
so it'll be interesting to see how the
next few episodes tie everything together

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:42.220
and solve some of our
most burning questions.

00:12:42.580 --> 00:12:44.000
Thanks for giving the video a watch.

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:46.160
Make sure to like and
subscribe with the bell on.

00:12:46.340 --> 00:12:50.180
I have a lot more AHS videos on the
way, so you don't want to miss it.

00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:53.080
Be sure to leave your comments
and theories about the show below,

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:56.800
and you can also reach out to
me on Twitter @ThinkStoryYT.

00:12:56.980 --> 00:12:58.460
Until next time remember,

00:12:58.460 --> 00:12:59.860
Daddy loves you very much.

